<p><FONT face="verdana, tahoma" size="2" >I'm not much for organized religion here, but do acknowledge it CAN serve a purpose in one's life.<br>
<br>
You see me (on occasion) kick the word "Pantheism" about.  That's kind of where I lie.  It's the belief that "God" (for lack of a better descriptor) is in everything.  Everything you see, touch, etc. is part of "God."  It's an old Greek thing, from what I understand, but it best fits the way I see things.<br>
<br>
I was raised Lutheran (Protestant Christian stuff), and was not much into it.  Churches were filled with politics and lots of answers you couldn't question.  After I was no longer forced to go to church (after I moved out), I began an in-depth study of Eastern religions (Buddhism, Taoism, Sufiism, Sikhism, some Muslim readings, etc.) and formed my own opinions on things.  Was big into meditiation and contemplation on life itself.<br>
<br>
Nowdays, I'm a bit more of a free spirit.  I read the writings of the "Christian Mystics" of the Middle Ages and assorted Koans (Zen Buddhism) when I need to kick my brain in another direction.  I take things as they are and go from there...<br>
<br>
But ah well.  I'm sure I'll comment more as this thread gets longer.  <img src="images/smilies/smile.gif" border=0><br>
<br>
Minvaren</font></p>

